[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2453512085","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/98800#issuecomment-2453512085","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/98800","id":2453512085,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6SPZ-V","user":{"login":"fuzzybinary","id":249982,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI0OTk4Mg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/249982?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fuzzybinary","html_url":"https://github.com/fuzzybinary","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fuzzybinary/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fuzzybinary/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fuzzybinary/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fuzzybinary/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fuzzybinary/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fuzzybinary/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fuzzybinary/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fuzzybinary/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fuzzybinary/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-03T17:57:09Z","updated_at":"2024-11-03T17:57:09Z","body":"From research - \r\n\r\nThe reason this happens is because the `ScriptCreateDialog` only references the theme, and (so far as I know) GDExtensions don't currently have a way to add icons to the theme. ([Relevant code](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/1bffd6c73b44b85e5889f54e14b2193940cf5bb1/editor/script_create_dialog.cpp#L132))\r\n\r\nThe `EditorNode`, on the other hand, asks the extension for the script's icon ([Relevant code](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/1bffd6c73b44b85e5889f54e14b2193940cf5bb1/editor/editor_node.cpp#L4770)).\r\n\r\nThe easy way forward here is to just make `ScriptCreateDialog` follow a similar approach as `EditorNode`, and look to see if the icon is defined in the Script's extension first.  \r\n\r\nThe harder way forward is to support GDExtensions adding theme icons probably....","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2453512085/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2504051199","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/98800#issuecomment-2504051199","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/98800","id":2504051199,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6VQMn_","user":{"login":"KoBeWi","id":2223172,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMjMxNzI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2223172?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi","html_url":"https://github.com/KoBeWi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-27T14:41:22Z","updated_at":"2024-11-27T14:41:22Z","body":"> The harder way forward is to support GDExtensions adding theme icons probably....\n\nModules can already add icons, so I think it makes sense for GDExtensions. How custom types register their icons normally?","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2504051199/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2505117463","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/98800#issuecomment-2505117463","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/98800","id":2505117463,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6VUQ8X","user":{"login":"fuzzybinary","id":249982,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI0OTk4Mg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/249982?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fuzzybinary","html_url":"https://github.com/fuzzybinary","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fuzzybinary/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fuzzybinary/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fuzzybinary/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fuzzybinary/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fuzzybinary/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fuzzybinary/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fuzzybinary/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fuzzybinary/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fuzzybinary/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-28T01:59:44Z","updated_at":"2024-11-28T01:59:44Z","body":"So far as I can tell, certain areas of the code ask extensions if they have an icon for a particular type, which is registered in the `.gdextension` file.\n\nFor example, in my `.gdextension` file I have the following:\n\n```\n[icons]\n\nDartScript = \"res://godot_dart/logo_dart.svg\"\nDartHotReload = \"res://godot_dart/hot_reload.svg\"\n```\n\nCertain areas of the editor ask the extension system if they define an icon for a type (such as in [`EditorNode`](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/9aed9eca40127bcf21ecd71d25fe8809f345d9e3/editor/editor_node.cpp#L4818) , but others (like the `ScriptCreateDialog`) don't, and only ask the Theme.\n\nI think the larger refactor would be for the Theme to handle asking extensions. My PR is the simpler solution to have `ScriptCreateDialog` work more similarly to `EditorNode`.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2505117463/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]